1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,455
Grimlash: an ancient harvest god, reawakened, and hungry for a grim and bountiful

2
00:00:04,455 --> 00:00:04,865
harvest.

3
00:00:05,085 --> 00:00:06,365
Here's how he plays.

4
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:11,552
Sort the fifteen Harvest Madness cards by level into three decks, and shuffle each.

5
00:00:11,772 --> 00:00:15,748
Put the Harvest Madness marker on the start space of the track, outlined in orange,

6
00:00:15,748 --> 00:00:17,233
at the top of the Killer board.

7
00:00:18,067 --> 00:00:22,143
Madness gives you power, at a price. Whenever you see the pumpkin icon, move the

8
00:00:22,143 --> 00:00:23,315
marker one space right.

9
00:00:23,535 --> 00:00:27,489
When it reaches a new level, draw two cards from that level's deck, keep one and

10
00:00:27,489 --> 00:00:31,492
discard the other. Its ability lasts as long as you stay at that level or higher.

11
00:00:31,712 --> 00:00:35,509
But if Madness goes beyond Level Three, onto the skull, you lose immediately.

12
00:00:36,333 --> 00:00:40,402
When you resolve a heart, choose: recover health as normal, or move the Madness

13
00:00:40,402 --> 00:00:42,925
marker one space left for each heart. Never both.

14
00:00:43,145 --> 00:00:46,948
If you drop to a lower level, discard the card for the level you just left.

15
00:00:46,948 --> 00:00:49,483
If you climb back up, draw two and keep one again.

16
00:00:49,483 --> 00:00:51,764
If a deck runs short, reshuffle its discards.

17
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:56,887
For example, Thorn-Choked Veins at Level One raises your maximum health by one and

18
00:00:56,887 --> 00:01:01,122
heals one. Blood of the Reaper at Level Two lets you flip it and lose a health to

19
00:01:01,122 --> 00:01:05,357
reroll all your dice. One With the Land at Level Three adds three maximum health.

20
00:01:05,577 --> 00:01:09,975
Health bonuses go when the card is discarded, and any health above your new maximum

21
00:01:09,975 --> 00:01:10,399
is lost.

22
00:01:10,619 --> 00:01:13,809
Once-per-turn powers are used by flipping the card face down.

23
00:01:13,809 --> 00:01:15,483
Flip them back up in the Upkeep.

24
00:01:16,300 --> 00:01:19,494
Grimlash only moves one space with his normal Killer action.

25
00:01:19,494 --> 00:01:23,858
But a move icon on a Terror card moves him at full speed, and his speed depends on

26
00:01:23,858 --> 00:01:26,945
your current Harvest Madness level, as shown on his board.

27
00:01:27,767 --> 00:01:32,549
Fields of Madness, his Epic Dark Power: at Madness Level nought or one, roll one die

28
00:01:32,549 --> 00:01:34,884
fewer, minimum one. Level two, no change.

29
00:01:34,884 --> 00:01:36,364
Level three, one die more.

30
00:01:36,584 --> 00:01:40,734
Rite of the Old One: whenever your Madness reaches a new level, discard the next

31
00:01:40,734 --> 00:01:44,936
Terror card. Rite of the Corrupted: each Upkeep, Madness goes up one if it didn't

32
00:01:44,936 --> 00:01:45,715
rise that turn.

33
00:01:45,935 --> 00:01:50,340
Root-Bound Curse: whenever you resolve hearts, to heal or lower Madness, Grimlash

34
00:01:50,340 --> 00:01:53,657
recovers half that much, rounded up. It's his nastiest power.

35
00:01:54,467 --> 00:01:58,526
Minor powers: Flaming Eyes adds two Madness whenever he enters your space, and

36
00:01:58,526 --> 00:02:02,637
Burning Sickle deals one damage to every Victim with you whenever he hurts you.

37
00:02:02,857 --> 00:02:06,671
Finales: Withered Harbinger costs you a Time for every space he moves.

38
00:02:06,671 --> 00:02:09,340
Hunger of the Old Gods pulls Victims towards him.

39
00:02:09,340 --> 00:02:12,500
Ancient Abomination adds your Madness level to his attack.

40
00:02:12,720 --> 00:02:16,849
And the Epic God of Blood and Grain kills every Victim when revealed, then hunts you

41
00:02:16,849 --> 00:02:17,733
and attacks twice.

42
00:02:18,567 --> 00:02:22,705
A few tips. Higher Madness gives better powers, but the skull is an instant loss.

43
00:02:22,925 --> 00:02:26,061
When you get hearts, spend them on whichever track is closer to killing you.

44
00:02:26,281 --> 00:02:29,958
He's one of the easier killers: players win nearly eighty per cent of games.

45
00:02:29,958 --> 00:02:30,441
Good luck.

